# The Quota: the voices in a fight (combat/sim/barks.mjs BARK_KEYS). One line per situation key; the voice is
# the rule's, named as q_rules.lwd names it: OBEDIENCE (footing), WEARINESS (breath), NERVE (water rising),
# DISGUST (behind you), SHAME (a grab coming), DREAD (in the dark), VANITY (losing), and the four that hold
# ground with words, TENDERNESS, CONTEMPT, JEALOUSY and SPITE.
# Before this file the slice had no @bark records, so its fights spoke the engine's placeholder lines and Lamp
# Quay's tide and eel-oil. 2026-11-16. Barks are one breath long, say what the body or the nose knows, and
# name no place or person a given era might not have.

@bark qb.frost1
key: footing.frost
text: Ice under the snow. Heel down first, as you were taught.

@bark qb.frost2
key: footing.frost
text: Frost on the setts. Short steps. Do as you're told and stay up.

@bark qb.frost3
key: footing.frost
text: It's glass under there. Don't go down in front of them.

@bark qb.wet1
key: footing.wet
text: Slush. Whole foot down.

@bark qb.wet2
key: footing.wet
text: Wet setts. They'll have your feet before he does.

@bark qb.wet3
key: footing.wet
text: Muck and meltwater. Stand where you're put and don't shift.

@bark qb.breath1
key: breath.low
text: We're blown. Back off a step. Please. Just a step.

@bark qb.breath2
key: breath.low
text: Oh, the chest. Let him come to us for once.

@bark qb.breath3
key: breath.low
text: Arms like wet sacks. We need to sit down. We can't.

@bark qb.water1
key: tide.near
text: Water across the yard. Go now, before it's at your boots.

@bark qb.water2
key: tide.near
text: The ground's going to soup behind you. Go first. Go now.

@bark qb.water3
key: tide.near
text: The drain's backing up. Off the low stones. Now.

@bark qb.smell1
key: smell.behind
text: Wet wool and sick. Behind you.

@bark qb.smell2
key: smell.behind
text: Lamp oil and somebody's dinner coming back up. Right behind.

@bark qb.smell3
key: smell.behind
text: Tallow and sweat. He's at your back.

@bark qb.grab1
key: tell.grab
text: He's after your collar. He wants you held for the others.

@bark qb.grab2
key: tell.grab
text: Hands open, coming in low. He wants you held where nobody can see your face.

@bark qb.grab3
key: tell.grab
text: He's looking at your coat, not your face.

@bark qb.dark1
key: dark.near
text: Somebody breathing past the lamp. It's started already.

@bark qb.dark2
key: dark.near
text: Boots in the snow, close. You knew this was coming.

@bark qb.dark3
key: dark.near
text: Gone quiet on your left. Here it comes.

@bark qb.pride1
key: pride.losing
text: Down in the muck, and the whole square looking at you.

@bark qb.pride2
key: pride.losing
text: Your good coat. Ruined. And look who saw it go.

@bark qb.pride3
key: pride.losing
text: They'll be telling this one in the Sheaf for years.

@bark qb.tender1
key: words.condolence
text: He's crying under all that. Tell him you know.

@bark qb.tender2
key: words.condolence
text: He's somebody's lad. Say his name if you know it.

@bark qb.tender3
key: words.condolence
text: He doesn't want this either. Tell him it can stop now.

@bark qb.tender4
key: words.condolence
text: Oh, look at his hands shaking. Say something gentle to him.

@bark qb.contempt1
key: words.formletter
text: Look at the state of him. Can't even hold it right. Tell him.

@bark qb.contempt2
key: words.formletter
text: Stand still. Let the little man see what he's swinging at.

@bark qb.contempt3
key: words.formletter
text: Out of his depth, this one. Make sure he knows it.

@bark qb.contempt4
key: words.formletter
text: Tell him to go home before he hurts himself.

@bark qb.jealous1
key: words.chit
text: Boots, a coat, a hot dinner in him. Ask him who went without.

@bark qb.jealous2
key: words.chit
text: You're the one who held back. Remind him who's owed.

@bark qb.jealous3
key: words.chit
text: He's never been hungry a day in his life. Say it.

@bark qb.jealous4
key: words.chit
text: He's got a warm house to go back to. You held back. He owes you.

@bark qb.spite1
key: words.hearsay
text: His mates are watching him lose. Say it loud, so it gets round.

@bark qb.spite2
key: words.hearsay
text: Tell the other one he's next. They'll all hear about who ran.

@bark qb.spite3
key: words.hearsay
text: Say his mother's name where they can all hear it.

@bark qb.spite4
key: words.hearsay
text: The one at the back's edging off. Shout it, so the whole street hears.
